00M due to award in Q1 2027.\n  - Norvane Utilities plans capex up 12%, with a C$450M tender due in Q2.\n  - VLTX won 60% of the last tender round.\n- **Data centres:** Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites. The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months. So demand is still growing, but at a slowing rate.\n- **VLTX order intake:** Utility orders have risen every quarter, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$640M, C$655M and then C$670M in 2026Q3.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- I haven't weighed each buyer's share of VLTX orders, because I didn't read the VLTX customer mix document.\n- The two tenders only matter if VLTX keeps winning. The 60% share is from the last round only.\n- Whether the utilities can finance this spending is a separate question that n3 is covering.\n\nSources: `utility-tenders`, `utility-capex-2027`, `datacentre-demand`, `grid-queue` and the `vltx_orders` series.","ttft_ms":1806,"type":"result","duration_ms":47817,"uuid":"3cef7d70-b02c-4f75-bc18-586eeaaf8a46","ttft_stream_ms":910,"time_to_request_ms":100,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":22,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":12,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":0,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":62,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":195,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":121,"process_rss_mib_result":202,"process_anon_mib_result":121,"process_peak_rss_mib":202,"process_cpu_ms_turn":689,"process_wall_ms_